<Project>

  <!-- The version numbers, kept in a file of their own so that raising them is not itself a change
       to Core: .github/scripts/check-versions.ps1 compares Core against its last release and
       leaves this file out.

       Releases are numbered from one sequence. Controls takes every number. Core takes a number
       only in a release that changes it, and then the same one as Controls, so Core may skip some:

         1.0.0  Controls 1.0.0  Core 1.0.0   first release
         1.0.1  Controls 1.0.1  Core 1.0.1   Core changed, so both
         1.0.2  Controls 1.0.2  Core 1.0.1   Controls alone
         1.0.3  Controls 1.0.3  Core 1.0.3   Core changed: the next free number, not 1.0.2

       So SumireVersion is the release, and the tag is v$(SumireVersion). SumireCoreVersion is
       either the same or the version of an earlier release, whose tag the same script diffs
       against.
       Controls names the Core it was built with as its minimum, because packing reads Core's own
       Version through the project reference, and the next major version of Controls as the bound
       (BoundCoreDependency in the Controls project). -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <SumireVersion>1.0.0</SumireVersion>
    <SumireCoreVersion>1.0.0</SumireCoreVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
